As you might already know, there is the "Community Over Code NA" conference
in October in Denver: https://communityovercode.org/.

Together with Isma=C3=ABl, for the 4th time in a row at 'Community Over Cod=
e"
series of events we are chairing the Data Engineering track at the event.
You can see all the talks that are planned - including Data Engineering
track at https://communityovercode.org/schedule/

The "Community Over Code" event is an opportunity to meet and talk to many
of the colleagues from other ASF projects and a great way to learn about
Apache Way from others - and also share your experiences. Onsite presence
is really different from watching talks remotely, the "Hallway" track is
usually one of the most interesting tracks at similar conferences, where
the talks and their content are mostly conversation openers.

I think it would also be great if you could promote the event on
your social media - website.

Example message for social media:

Join us October 7-10 for the Data Engineering track at Community Over Code
North America 2024. Register today at
https://communityovercode.org/registration/

And here is the way how you can add event promotion in your website
https://www.apachecon.com/event-images/

I hope we will see you at the event!

J. & I.

