Hi Lucas,

Yeah, I agree that it's not ideal to push the burden on users letting
them to remember when changes happen (and they need to consider what
kind of changes are "sensitive" enough), manually update the ID either
from a config or via something else --- mentioned it in your doc and
in my first comment as well, so I think we are on the same page.

I'm also on the path of some default impl would be needed, like
`hash(topology.describe())`, but then what I thought originally was
that --- unless topology.describe() has changed a lot since the last
time I reviewed it --- such auto-generated ID would not be 100 percent
sensitive (e.g. like you said in the comment if users just change the
threshold of a filter) anyways, so why not just make it catching the
most destructive changes only which would result in different set of
tasks, and then letting the handling logic of it be dump since such
cases would be rare. But now I get that our goal in the long run is
pushing it to be as sensitive as possible in catching all kinds of
changes.

With that I would drop my suggestion regarding the handling logic; I'd
only push that even in the long run, let's not throw ID generation to
the user's shoulders still. There's always something we can do
automatically, with source code hashing as the last reserve :)

Guozhang

