MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

hi Rich

Sorry for late response. I have just one comment:

Have we consider replacing `Headers` by `Iterable<Header>`? There are some di=
sadvantages of using `Headers`:

1. `Headers` have many setters and they are meaningless to users.=20
2. If users do want to modify `Headers`, they can get inconsistent results as=
 `Headers` can be either readonly of modifiable.

Best,
Chia-Ping

On 2024/07/23 03:13:59 "Rich C." wrote:
> Hi Everyone,
>=20
> I hope this email finds you well.
>=20
> I would like to start a discussion on KIP-512. The initial version of
> KIP-512 was created in 2019, and I have resurrected it in 2024 with more
> details about the motivation behind it.
>=20
> You can view the current version of the KIP here: KIP-512: Make Record
> Headers Available in onAcknowledgement.
> <https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-512%3A+make+Record+H=
eaders+available+in+onAcknowledgement>
>=20
> Let's focus on discussing the necessity of this feature first. If we agree
> on its importance, we can then move on to discussing the proposed changes.
>=20
> Looking forward to your feedback.
>=20
> Best regards,
> Rich
>=20

