Hi TengYao!

Sorry for being late to the discussion...

After reading the thread and then the KIP, I had a few =
questions/comments:

KT1: In Motivation, it states: "This scenario can result in the broker =
registering a new member for which it will never receive a proper leave =
request.=E2=80=9D Just to be clear, the broker will always have cases =
where it might lose connection with a member. That=E2=80=99s not unique =
to the initial heartbeat, right?

KT2: There was a bit of back and forth about format of the member ID. =
=46rom what I gathered in the thread, the member ID is still defined in =
the RPC as a string and not a UUID, right? The KIP states that the =
=E2=80=9Cclient must generate a UUID as the member ID=E2=80=9D and that =
the =E2=80=9Cserver will validate that a valid UUID is provided.=E2=80=9D =
Is that a change for the server, or is it already enforced as a UUID?

KT3: Lianet mentioned some confusion over the use of the word =
=E2=80=9Csession.=E2=80=9D Isn=E2=80=99t =E2=80=9Csession=E2=80=9D =
synonymous with =E2=80=9Cmembership?=E2=80=9D

KT4: Under =E2=80=9CMember ID Lifecycle,=E2=80=9D it states: "The client =
should reuse the same UUID as the member ID for all heartbeats and =
rejoin attempts to maintain continuity within the group.=E2=80=9D Could =
we change the first part of that to =E2=80=9CThe Consumer instance =
should=E2=80=A6=E2=80=9D We do have lifetimes that extend past the =
lifetime of a client instance (such as the transaction ID).

Thanks,
Kirk

