Hi Maxim,

Server-side interceptors for messages have been discussed several times,=
 but the KIP never got accepted. People often pushed back on what they s=
aw as the risks and performance problems of allowing user-supplied code =
in the hot path of accepting records.

Your KIP is a bit different because it just specifies accessing the Prod=
uceRequest. But I think you still have similar problems. What happens if=
 the user-supplied code crashes or takes a long time? If we change the f=
ormat of ProduceRequest, is it acceptable for all these interceptors to =
start failing?

I suspect that if we ever add server-side interceptors, we'll want to gi=
ve access to records, not to internal data structures like Requests. Thi=
s could involve a big performance hit, but perhaps people will be willin=
g to pay it.

best,
Colin


