Hi Maxim,

The issue is not the number of lines of code, but the need to support th=
is indefinitely in the future. For example, if we want to move to a new =
request type that is different than ProduceRequest, or create a new vers=
ion of ProduceRequest, we wouldn't be able to do that in the future whil=
e maintaining the compatibility promised in this KIP. So this would be a=
 very significant constraint on development, which we probably wouldn't =
adopt unless there was no other way forward.

best,
Colin

